# One byte sequence for a newline, on every checkout.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true, so without this a Windows clone gets every text file with
# CRLF line endings. That is not cosmetic here: the shipped example workspace is copied verbatim into a new
# workspace and its bytes are what tests compare and what documents hash to; a shell script checked out with
# CRLF fails inside a container with `\r: command not found`; and every diff between a Windows clone and a
# Linux one becomes the whole file. LF everywhere means the repository is the same repository on all three
# platforms in CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# And these are bytes, not text — Git must never look for a newline in them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.sqlite binary
